  "note": "PHASE 1.5I, TYLER'S RULING: THAD WALKS ONLY IN FRONT OF THIS RAIL. Dual-side navigation is retired -- 1.5G gave the rear ground back, 1.5H made the fence uncrossable, and Tyler could still put him in the rail, because the rear strip mud_mid_3 (x 2268-2614, y 690-776) was legal ground and standing there IS standing in the fence. `rect` is the ground that is no longer player ground: the whole rear of the rail's span, from the top of the far mud (600) down to the top of the front band (816). It is not an overlay the router may route around -- the compiler carves it out, so no walk box exists there at all. `resolveBelowY` is the line a click inside `rect` resolves BELOW: the engine restricts the landing to boxes at or under it, so a click on the bar, on a post, or on the ground behind them puts him on the nearest FRONT-side ground rather than sending him round the block to the boardwalk. `posts` are the two footprints his feet must clear by `minPostClearance`; the far post's foot is at 812 and the front band starts at 816, which is 4 px, so its safety notch carries the front ground down to 824 there. tools/gauntlet/rail-front-only.mjs clicks all of this like a player and asserts he is never inside `rect`."
